# Template for Azure hosting configuration in a new region
# To add hosting to a new region, follow these steps:
#
# 1. Create a network.hcl file in the region directory with appropriate CIDR blocks:
#    ```hcl
#    # Network configuration for Azure [region] region
#    
#    locals {
#      # VNet CIDR block for [region]
#      address_space = ["10.17.X.0/23"]  # Replace X with appropriate value
#      
#      # Subnet configurations specific to [region]
#      subnets = {
#        "az1-node-subnet" = {
#          address_prefixes  = ["10.17.X.0/26"]  # Replace X with appropriate value
#          service_endpoints = ["Microsoft.Storage", "Microsoft.KeyVault", "Microsoft.ContainerRegistry"]
#        },
#        "az1-endpoint-subnet" = {
#          address_prefixes  = ["10.17.X.80/28"]  # Replace X with appropriate value
#          service_endpoints = ["Microsoft.Storage", "Microsoft.Sql", "Microsoft.KeyVault"]
#        }
#      }
#    }
#    ```
#
# 2. Copy the hosting-shell.hcl.template to your region's hosting/terragrunt.hcl file.
#    The shell is designed to be identical across all regions and will automatically
#    pick up the network configuration from your region's network.hcl file.
#
# See existing regions like eastus, westus, or northeurope for examples.